{
    "background_story": "Alonso was a skilled luthier who spent his days crafting beautiful guitars in his small workshop. He was particularly fascinated by the work of Charles H. Dawes, the inventor of the Dawes guitar amplifier. Inspired by Dawes' innovative designs, Alonso set out to create his own custom amplifiers that would complement his handmade instruments. As word of his exceptional craftsmanship spread, musicians from all over the city flocked to his shop, seeking his expertise. Alonso's dedication to his craft and his passion for the work of Dawes earned him a reputation as one of the finest luthiers in the country. His instruments and amplifiers were sought after by musicians who valued their unique tone and exceptional quality.",
